<title>USA: Tracor unit gets government contract.</title>
<headline>Tracor unit gets government contract.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A unit of Tracor Inc said Tuesday it had been awarded a contract worth about $55 million to provide commercial, off-the-shelf computer hardware and software to the U.S. Department of Defense.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded to Cordant, a subsidiary of Tracor unit Tracor Information Systems Co.</p>
<p>The company said the ultimate aim of the contract is to help military medical treatment facilities in the delivery of quality patient care.</p>
